{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/k3y5ov21","slide":15,"name":"object 3","text":"THE DATA\n\n\nNHS PROMs national data pack, knee replacement cohort,\nanonymised at source\nOne row per patient episode; roughly 46,000 procedures a year\nacross the collection window\nPre-operative questionnaire: Oxford Knee Score 0–48 with pain, function and ADL subscales; EQ-5D-3L; symptom period; previous surgery; living arrangements; mobility\nTwelve comorbidity flags\nProvider dimension joined in: ODS code, university / independent\nstatus\nPost-operative OKS at six months — when the patient returns the\nquestionnaire","textPreview":"THE DATA |  |  | NHS PROMs national data pack, knee replacement cohort, | anonymised at source | One row per patient episode; roughly 46,...","textChars":517,"textLines":13,"bbox":[85.83,179.41,495.8,340.53]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/76p4jqls","slide":15,"name":"object 4","text":"THE PREDICTION","textPreview":"THE PREDICTION","textChars":14,"textLines":1,"bbox":[677.65,179.41,162.6,22.27]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/65gnqlk7","slide":15,"name":"object 5","text":"Inputs are pre-operative only — everything knowable before the\ndecision to operate\nTarget is derived: oks_delta = oks_t1 − oks_t0\nThe positive class is the BAD outcome — the patient who does not meaningfully improve, because that is the class worth detecting\n~45 features after encoding\n\n\nAnonymised, national, already public-sector governed. Every interesting problem is downstream of that.\n\n\n[TODO: settle the target definition and prevalence — see notes]","textPreview":"Inputs are pre-operative only — everything knowable before the | decision to operate | Target is derived: oks_delta = oks_t1 − oks_t0 | T...","textChars":457,"textLines":11,"bbox":[677.65,240.95,497.73,288.6]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/vaxsvy10","slide":15,"text":""}
